      en: "The Monumento al Indio in Trinidad is an 8-meter-tall bronze statue depicting an indigenous man. Created by sculptor Emiliano Luján in 1941, it stands on a stone pedestal. The monument symbolizes Bolivia's indigenous peoples. Located at the entrance to Trinidad, it is a key cultural symbol for the Beni region. It is a popular photo spot. A small park surrounds the monument.",
